                  "value": {
                    "stringValue": "An **agent trace** is a record of what an AI agent did while handling a task. It often includes the steps it took, such as:\n\n- the user\u2019s request and the agent\u2019s inputs\n- actions or tool calls the agent made\n- results returned by tools\n- decisions or status updates\n- the final response\n\nFor example, a trace for \u201cWhat\u2019s the weather in Paris?\u201d might show the agent calling a weather service, receiving the forecast, and then replying.\n\nTraces are useful for debugging, auditing, and understanding how a task was completed. They don\u2019t necessarily include the model\u2019s full internal reasoning; often they show only observable steps and tool interactions."
